  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758876,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1 Year Radius - Commodore 64\n\nPrepare for a chilling descent into paranoia and psychological horror in *1 Year Radius*, a unique and unsettling adventure for the Commodore 64. You awaken with amnesia in a seemingly deserted, decaying town, the year being 1984. A cryptic radio message reveals a terrifying truth: a localized temporal anomaly is shrinking, compressing the last year of existence into a rapidly diminishing area. \n\nAs the radius closes, the town's inhabitants – or what remains of them – reappear, trapped in repeating loops of their final days. Your mission is to uncover the cause of the anomaly and, crucially, to understand your own forgotten role in this unfolding disaster. \n\nExplore the eerie, pixelated streets, interact with fragmented memories and unsettling characters, and solve intricate puzzles that unravel the mystery. The game features a haunting soundtrack and a deliberately unsettling atmosphere, emphasizing psychological tension over action. Can you break free from the shrinking radius and reclaim your lost memories before time runs out?"
    },
